response.output:
I'll break down this feature into epics and stories with acceptance criteria.

```json
{
  "item": "DP-61",
  "epics": [
    {
      "id": "E1",
      "title": "Product Identity Model",
      "stories": [
        {
          "id": "E1.S1",
          "statement": "As a user, I want ingredients to store product identity (barcode, brand, package size) so that I can track real branded products in my pantry",
          "domains": ["backend"],
          "acceptance_criteria": [
            {
              "id": "E1.S1.AC1",
              "given": "the ingredient schema is defined",
              "when": "I add optional fields: brand (string), barcode (string), packageQuantity (number), packageUnit (string)",
              "then": "barcode is unique when present and enforced at the database level"
            },
            {
              "id": "E1.S1.AC2",
              "given": "an ingredient with product identity fields populated",
              "when": "I query the ingredient",
              "then": "barcode, brand, packageQuantity, and packageUnit are all returned"
            },
            {
              "id": "E1.S1.AC3",
              "given": "two ingredients exist",
              "when": "I try to create a third ingredient with the same barcode as the first",
              "then": "the creation fails with a barcode uniqueness constraint error"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "E2",
      "title": "One-Step Pantry Item Creation",
      "stories": [
        {
          "id": "E2.S1",
          "statement": "As a user, I want to create a branded pantry item in one step from the pantry page so that I don't have to navigate between /ingredients/new and /pantry",
          "domains": ["ux", "backend"],
          "acceptance_criteria": [
            {
              "id": "E2.S1.AC1",
              "given": "I'm on the /pantry page",
              "when": "I click the 'Create custom item' button",
              "then": "a modal or form opens with fields for ingredient name, barcode, brand, package quantity/unit, and initial pantry quantity"
            },
            {
              "id": "E2.S1.AC2",
              "given": "the creation form is open",
              "when": "I fill in ingredient name, brand, barcode, and pantry quantity and submit",
              "then": "a Server Action creates the ingredient and its pantry row in a single transaction"
            },
            {
              "id": "E2.S1.AC3",
              "given": "the ingredient and pantry row are created successfully",
              "when": "the Server Action completes",
              "then": "the pantry page refreshes and displays the new item with its product identity visible"
            },
            {
              "id": "E2.S1.AC4",
              "given": "I'm creating a custom item without a barcode",
              "when": "I submit the form with barcode left empty",
              "then": "the item is created successfully without a barcode"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "E3",
      "title": "Zero-Quantity Pantry Support",
      "stories": [
        {
          "id": "E3.S1",
          "statement": "As a user, I want pantry rows to allow zero quantity so that running out of a product doesn't erase it from my pantry",
          "domains": ["backend", "ux"],
          "acceptance_criteria": [
            {
              "id": "E3.S1.AC1",
              "given": "a pantry row with quantity > 0",
              "when": "I reduce the quantity to 0",
              "then": "the pantry row remains in the database and is not deleted"
            },
            {
              "id": "E3.S1.AC2",
              "given": "the pantry validation logic currently enforces quantity > 0",
              "when": "I update the schema to allow quantity >= 0",
              "then": "pantry rows with quantity = 0 are valid and can be persisted"
            },
            {
              "id": "E3.S1.AC3",
              "given": "I create a pantry row with quantity = 0 via the one-step creation form",
              "when": "the form is submitted",
              "then": "the row is created successfully with quantity = 0"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "E3.S2",
          "statement": "As a user, I want to see an 'out of stock' state for pantry items with zero quantity so that I can quickly identify what I need to restock",
          "domains": ["ux"],
          "acceptance_criteria": [
            {
              "id": "E3.S2.AC1",
              "given": "a pantry item has quantity = 0",
              "when": "I view the pantry list",
              "then": "the item renders with an 'out of stock' visual state (e.g., grayed out, labeled, or moved to a separate section)"
            },
            {
              "id": "E3.S2.AC2",
              "given": "I'm viewing a pantry item detail page with quantity = 0",
              "when": "the page loads",
              "then": "the quantity field displays 0 and an 'out of stock' label is visible"
            },
            {
              "id": "E3.S2.AC3",
              "given": "a pantry item transitions from quantity > 0 to quantity = 0",
              "when": "I update the quantity",
              "then": "the visual state changes to 'out of stock' immediately"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "E4",
      "title": "Product Identity Display",
      "stories": [
        {
          "id": "E4.S1",
          "statement": "As a user, I want to see and edit product identity fields (barcode, brand, package size) on the ingredient form so that I can capture and update product details",
          "domains": ["ux"],
          "acceptance_criteria": [
            {
              "id": "E4.S1.AC1",
              "given": "I'm on the ingredient creation or edit form",
              "when": "the form renders",
              "then": "I see optional input fields for brand, barcode, packageQuantity, and packageUnit alongside the ingredient name"
            },
            {
              "id": "E4.S1.AC2",
              "given": "I edit an ingredient with existing product identity",
              "when": "I load the form",
              "then": "the barcode, brand, and package fields are pre-populated with their current values"
            },
            {
              "id": "E4.S1.AC3",
              "given": "I update the barcode field to a new value",
              "when": "I save the ingredient",
              "then": "the barcode uniqueness constraint is checked and the update succeeds or fails appropriately"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "E4.S2",
          "statement": "As a user, I want to see product identity on the pantry page so that I can verify which branded product I'm tracking",
          "domains": ["ux"],
          "acceptance_criteria": [
            {
              "id": "E4.S2.AC1",
              "given": "a pantry item has brand and barcode populated",
              "when": "I view the pantry list or detail page",
              "then": "the brand, barcode, and package size are displayed (e.g., 'Ritz crackers, Barcode: 12345, 14 oz')"
            },
            {
              "id": "E4.S2.AC2",
              "given": "a pantry item has no barcode",
              "when": "I view the pantry page",
              "then": "the item displays the brand and package size without attempting to show a blank barcode field"
            },
            {
              "id": "E4.S2.AC3",
              "given": "I click on a pantry item detail",
              "when": "the detail page loads",
              "then": "all product identity fields are visible in a dedicated section"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

This breakdown spans 4 epics and 6 stories:

1. **Product Identity Model** — foundational schema changes
2. **One-Step Creation** — UX improvement for the primary workflow
3. **Zero-Quantity Support** — removing the quantity constraint and showing "out of stock"
4. **Product Identity Display** — surfacing the new fields in the UI

The stories are sequenced by dependency: the model work (E1) enables the one-step creation (E2), which benefits from zero-quantity support (E3), with display (E4) layered across the UI surfaces. Each acceptance criterion is testable and grounded in the observable behavior.

