```json
{
  "item": "HM-40",
  "epics": [
    {
      "id": "HM-40-E1",
      "title": "Authentication infrastructure",
      "stories": [
        {
          "id": "HM-40-S1",
          "statement": "As a system administrator, I want bearer tokens to be parsed and validated on every incoming request",
          "domains": ["backend", "auth"],
          "acceptance_criteria": [
            {
              "id": "HM-40-AC1",
              "given": "a request with an Authorization header containing a bearer token",
              "when": "the request is processed",
              "then": "the bearer token is extracted and validated"
            },
            {
              "id": "HM-40-AC2",
              "given": "a request with an invalid or malformed bearer token",
              "when": "the request is processed",
              "then": "the request is rejected with a 401 Unauthorized response"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "HM-40-S2",
          "statement": "As a system administrator, I want API keys to be stored as salted hashes and validated on request",
          "domains": ["backend", "auth"],
          "acceptance_criteria": [
            {
              "id": "HM-40-AC3",
              "given": "an API key is configured in the system",
              "when": "the key is stored",
              "then": "it is hashed with a cryptographic salt (bcrypt, scrypt, or PBKDF2)"
            },
            {
              "id": "HM-40-AC4",
              "given": "a request provides an API key",
              "when": "the request is processed",
              "then": "the provided key is hashed and compared against the stored hash"
            },
            {
              "id": "HM-40-AC5",
              "given": "a request with an invalid API key",
              "when": "the request is processed",
              "then": "the request is rejected with a 401 Unauthorized response"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "HM-40-S3",
          "statement": "As a developer, I want authenticated requests to resolve to a Principal with tenantId and scopes",
          "domains": ["backend", "auth"],
          "acceptance_criteria": [
            {
              "id": "HM-40-AC6",
              "given": "a valid bearer token or API key is provided",
              "when": "the request is authenticated",
              "then": "a Principal object is created containing tenantId and an array of scopes"
            },
            {
              "id": "HM-40-AC7",
              "given": "a request with an authenticated Principal",
              "when": "downstream handlers access the request context",
              "then": "the Principal is available and contains correct tenantId and scopes without re-parsing"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "HM-40-E2",
      "title": "Tenant isolation via resource namespacing",
      "stories": [
        {
          "id": "HM-40-S4",
          "statement": "As a system architect, I want topic and subscription IDs to be transparently namespaced by tenant at the API boundary",
          "domains": ["backend", "multi-tenancy"],
          "acceptance_criteria": [
            {
              "id": "HM-40-AC8",
              "given": "a request from tenantA to create a topic named 'my-topic'",
              "when": "the topic is persisted",
              "then": "the internal storage key is namespaced (e.g., 'tenantA::my-topic') to guarantee uniqueness"
            },
            {
              "id": "HM-40-AC9",
              "given": "a request from tenantA to read topic 'my-topic'",
              "when": "the API receives the request",
              "then": "the topic ID is automatically prefixed with tenantA's namespace before any storage lookup"
            },
            {
              "id": "HM-40-AC10",
              "given": "the Principal in the request context",
              "when": "any resource is looked up",
              "then": "the lookup is transparently scoped to the Principal's tenantId by the API layer"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "HM-40-S5",
          "statement": "As a tenant user, I want to be unable to access another tenant's resources even if I know their identifiers",
          "domains": ["backend", "multi-tenancy", "security"],
          "acceptance_criteria": [
            {
              "id": "HM-40-AC11",
              "given": "tenantA is authenticated and tenantB has a topic 'shared-topic'",
              "when": "tenantA attempts to access 'shared-topic' or 'tenantB::shared-topic'",
              "then": "the request returns 404 Not Found (resource does not exist from tenantA's perspective)"
            },
            {
              "id": "HM-40-AC12",
              "given": "a list-topics request from tenantA",
              "when": "the request is processed",
              "then": "only topics in tenantA's namespace are returned; tenantB's topics are never visible"
            },
            {
              "id": "HM-40-AC13",
              "given": "a list-subscriptions request from tenantA",
              "when": "the request is processed",
              "then": "only subscriptions in tenantA's namespace are returned"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "HM-40-E3",
      "title": "Authorization enforcement across REST and gRPC",
      "stories": [
        {
          "id": "HM-40-S6",
          "statement": "As a system administrator, I want all REST endpoints to require authentication except /health and /metrics",
          "domains": ["backend", "auth", "rest"],
          "acceptance_criteria": [
            {
              "id": "HM-40-AC14",
              "given": "a request to a protected REST endpoint without credentials",
              "when": "the request is processed",
              "then": "it is rejected with a 401 Unauthorized response"
            },
            {
              "id": "HM-40-AC15",
              "given": "an unauthenticated request to /health",
              "when": "the request is processed",
              "then": "it succeeds and returns the health status (no authentication required)"
            },
            {
              "id": "HM-40-AC16",
              "given": "an unauthenticated request to /metrics",
              "when": "the request is processed",
              "then": "it succeeds and returns metrics data (no authentication required)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "HM-40-S7",
          "statement": "As a system administrator, I want all gRPC endpoints to require authentication",
          "domains": ["backend", "auth", "grpc"],
          "acceptance_criteria": [
            {
              "id": "HM-40-AC17",
              "given": "a gRPC call without bearer token or API key",
              "when": "the call is processed",
              "then": "it is rejected with gRPC Unauthenticated status"
            },
            {
              "id": "HM-40-AC18",
              "given": "a gRPC call with valid credentials",
              "when": "the call is processed",
              "then": "the call proceeds and the Principal is available in the handler context"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "HM-40-S8",
          "statement": "As a system administrator, I want admin operations to require an admin scope",
          "domains": ["backend", "auth", "authorization"],
          "acceptance_criteria": [
            {
              "id": "HM-40-AC19",
              "given": "a Principal without 'admin' scope",
              "when": "the Principal attempts an admin operation (delete topic, delete subscription, etc.)",
              "then": "the request is rejected with a 403 Forbidden response"
            },
            {
              "id": "HM-40-AC20",
              "given": "a Principal with 'admin' scope",
              "when": "the Principal attempts an admin operation",
              "then": "the operation proceeds normally"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "HM-40-E4",
      "title": "Configuration, fail-fast defaults, and backward compatibility",
      "stories": [
        {
          "id": "HM-40-S9",
          "statement": "As an operator, I want authentication to be configurable with fail-fast defaults",
          "domains": ["backend", "configuration"],
          "acceptance_criteria": [
            {
              "id": "HM-40-AC21",
              "given": "the system starts with no explicit auth configuration",
              "when": "the system initializes",
              "then": "it defaults to fail-fast mode: all requests require authentication and fail if not provided"
            },
            {
              "id": "HM-40-AC22",
              "given": "invalid or incomplete auth configuration is provided",
              "when": "the system starts",
              "then": "it fails with a clear error message (e.g., missing API key configuration) rather than degrading silently"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "HM-40-S10",
          "statement": "As a developer, I want an auth-disabled mode for local development",
          "domains": ["backend", "configuration"],
          "acceptance_criteria": [
            {
              "id": "HM-40-AC23",
              "given": "the system is configured with auth disabled (e.g., AUTH_MODE=disabled or AUTH_DISABLED=true)",
              "when": "the system starts",
              "then": "all endpoints accept requests without authentication"
            },
            {
              "id": "HM-40-AC24",
              "given": "auth-disabled mode is active",
              "when": "a request is processed",
              "then": "the system creates a default Principal with a default tenantId and development scopes (e.g., 'admin')"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "HM-40-S11",
          "statement": "As an operator, I want backward compatibility with existing single-tenant deployments",
          "domains": ["backend", "compatibility"],
          "acceptance_criteria": [
            {
              "id": "HM-40-AC25",
              "given": "an existing single-tenant HermesMQ deployment with topics and subscriptions",
              "when": "the system is upgraded with authentication enabled",
              "then": "there is a clear migration path to assign existing resources to a designated default tenant"
            },
            {
              "id": "HM-40-AC26",
              "given": "existing clients continue to use previously-configured API keys",
              "when": "the system is upgraded",
              "then": "the API keys are migrated to the new hashed storage format with no client-side changes required"
            },
            {
              "id": "HM-40-AC27",
              "given": "the system is in backward-compatibility mode",
              "when": "requests are processed",
              "then": "they behave as single-tenant (all resources belong to the default tenant) until multi-tenant configuration is enabled"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

**Decomposition summary:**

- **E1** sets up the core auth layer (tokens, keys, Principals) — implement first
- **E2** builds tenant isolation via namespacing — depends on E1
- **E3** enforces auth across REST/gRPC surfaces and applies authorization rules — depends on E1
- **E4** adds configuration, dev modes, and migration story — can be largely parallel but needs the others to be testable

Each story is testable and independent enough to assign to a developer. The acceptance criteria are concrete (given/when/then) and avoid implementation details.

