**Recommended sequence:** list → inspect → selective redrive → bulk redrive. Operator discovery (listing) ships first; inspection should land before or alongside redrive so operators can verify a failure reason; selective redrive validates the core idempotency and in-flight isolation guarantees before bulk redrive builds on them at higher volume.

**Key constraints built into acceptance criteria:**
- **Idempotency** (ac-3 in both redrive stories) — redriving the same message twice doesn't create duplicates
- **In-flight safety** (ac-4 in both redrive stories) — active deliveries are unaffected by recovery operations
- **Resilient to stale state** (selective redrive ac-2, bulk redrive ac-2) — already-redriven or missing messages don't fail the whole operation

**Open questions to clarify before implementation:** auth gating, page size limits/defaults, bulk-redrive message count bounds, and retention window for delivery-attempt history.

